ns: considered moody, regarded as a loner. Also \"hot temper\" and \"know-it-all\" from shared mental model, but those are from Agent 2's notes. Our own notes include \"considered moody\" and \"loner\". Those are concerns for crew cooperation.\n\nCandidate B: very conscientious, handles stress well, good at assessing weather, excellent computer skills. Concerns: pretentious, sometimes adopts wrong tone. Also \"makes nasty remarks\" from shared mental model, but not in our notes. We have \"pretentious\" and \"wrong tone\". So B has reliability and stress resilience but communication concerns.\n\nCandidate C: makes correct decisions quickly, difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric, not willing to further education, puts concern for others above everything, excellent attention skills. So C has decision quality, attention, but communication and adaptability concerns.\n\nCandidate A: anticipates dangerous situations, sees complex connections, excellent spatial vision, very good leadership qualities, unfriendly, eats unhealthily. So A has technical competence and leadership but interpersonal concerns.\n\nWe need to decide. D seems strong technically and responsibility, but moody and loner may affect crew cooperation. B is conscientious and stress resilient but pretentious and wrong tone. Which is better? Probably D still best overall.\n\nThus we can support D, but we should note concerns and argue why strengths outweigh.\n\nWe'll produce public message: recommend D, reference strengths and concerns, compare to others.\n\nMETADATA_JSON vote D.\n\nProceed."}
